  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nAn upper level disturbance is moving eastward across southern\nCanada this morning. Thus some light rain showers are affecting\nareas along the Highway 2 corridor from east of Shelby to Harlem.\nThese showers should exit the area by 9 AM or so. Patchy fog has\nalso developed over North Central MT as well this morning. This\nfog should burn off by mid morning as well.\n\nOn Thursday, the next upper level trof approaches from the west. A\nsouthwest flow over Central MT develops, resulting in an unstable\nairmass by Thu afternoon. Expect several rounds of\nshowers/thunderstorms over Southwest/Central MT from Thursday\nevening through Fri. Some storms could be on the strong side. The\nprecipitation will be a bit slow to exit, with showers continuing\ninto Saturday.\n\nFor Sunday and Monday, and upper level ridge builds over the CWA,\nresulting in drier and mild conditions.\n\nFor next Tue/Wed...the forecast models are struggling on a\nsolution, as both models differ from one another.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nThe main concern for the thunderstorms Thu night and Friday will\nbe how strong will the thunderstorms be. Some storms could produce\nstrong wind gusts and hail. Instability of CAPE could exceed 1500\nj/kg around Helena on Friday. Additionally, the airmass will \nremain unstable Thu night for thunderstorms to likely continue \nmuch of Thursday night.\n\nFor next Tue...both the GFS/EC models continue to have opposite\nsolutions, with one model warm/dry...the other model cold/wet.\nThus confidence is low at this time for next Tue. Brusda",
